{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Aaron took, as, etc.</b> Meaning — immediately adjacent to Moses' utterance, to teach you that he did not delay even a moment. It further intends: since the matter here is the opposite of the law — to offer incense outside its time and outside its place — therefore it says <b>and Aaron took</b>, and the sense of ״וַיִּקַּח״ is ״as Moses spoke״ — meaning, by the word of a prophet. And a prophet is to be believed when he says to transgress one of the commandments of the Torah for the time being, as with Elijah on Mount Carmel (I Kings 18:30)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:36.224377143Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}